      "summary": "The fix handles nested blocks, but its raw brace counting can truncate valid Terraform blocks when a string contains a closing brace. This is a nonblocking false failure in the RELEASE-ID-06 contract test.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "minor",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/ReleaseIdentityContractTests.cs",
          "line": 321,
          "message": "The brace scanner counts braces inside quoted strings, so a valid role assignment description containing `}` can truncate the body before principal_id and scope are checked. Ignore braces inside strings and comments when finding the block boundary.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RoleAssignmentBlocks adjusts block depth for every brace character, including braces inside quoted strings. The RELEASE-ID-06 test uses the resulting body to check principal_id and scope.",
            "failureScenario": "If a valid role assignment has a description such as \"grants } access\" before its direct principal_id and scope attributes, the brace in the string ends the parsed body early. The test then reports the required attributes missing and fails despite both references being direct."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
