        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The parser now balances nested braces, addressing the previous finding in the implementation. However, no test protects that fix: reverting to the prior truncating parser would pass the current tests.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/ReleaseIdentityContractTests.cs",
          "line": 65,
          "message": "Add a regression case with a nested block before principal_id or scope so the contract test fails if assignment parsing stops at the first closing brace.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Role_assignments_use_only_direct_resource_references exercises RoleAssignmentBlocks against the repository Terraform files, but no test fixture includes a nested block before principal_id or scope.",
            "failureScenario": "If the balanced-brace parser is replaced by the previous regex, the suite still passes with the current Terraform files and fixtures. A role assignment with a nested block before an indirect principal_id or scope could then evade the contract check, leaving AC RELEASE-ID-06 unenforced."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
